#import "../helpers/shared.typ": req, budget, src, supply, pitfall
= Community Building <sec-community>
#budget(0.7, 420)

#req(source: "SOL §V.A + §VI.A criterion 3")[
*Community Building*: Describe plans to engage users and developers through activities
such as workshops, hackathons, competitions, and research networks. Criterion 3: does the
proposal clearly describe a recruitment strategy for new contributors to the ecosystem and
for growing the userbase?
]

#pitfall(source: "W1 @ 00:36:29")[
"This last piece is the recruitment strategy for your new contributors. How are you going
to grow your user base? This doesn't happen passively. So how are you going to bring new
contributors continuously to the system... Very, very deliberate kinds of actions."
Inadequate recruitment strategy is the third pitfall NSF names.
]

#pitfall(source: "W1 @ 00:36:29")[
"Be specific in your planning and evaluation. So as you write up your proposal, if you
just write generically... we need you to be very, very specific." Generic planning is the
fourth named pitfall.
]

#src("W1", "@ 00:36:00")[
Retention framing NSF uses: "How are you going to get their attention two years down the
road when this isn't the shiny new open source ecosystem? How are you going to continue to
have those contributors?"
]

#supply[
- Stage-by-stage pipeline design: first contribution → sustained → maintainer
- Response-time commitment on first contributions; entry-issue curation; mentorship model
- Documentation gap analysis sourced from interview + support-request evidence
- Support triage model and how load is distributed rather than concentrated
- Named events, each with target audience and stated recruitment goal
- A measurement per stage, against the §2 funnel baseline
]
